Source: Google Tsguide > Google TypeScript Style Guide > Language features > Classes > Class method declarations

#### Class method declarations

Class method declarations *must not* use a semicolon to separate individual
method declarations:

```
class Foo {
 doThing() {
 console.log("A");
 }
}
```
```
class Foo {
 doThing() {
 console.log("A");
 }; // <-- unnecessary
}
```
Method declarations should be separated from surrounding code by a single blank line:

```
class Foo {
 doThing() {
 console.log("A");
 }
 getOtherThing(): number {
 return 4;
 }
}
```
```
class Foo {
 doThing() {
 console.log("A");
 }
 getOtherThing(): number {
 return 4;
 }
}
```

