Source: Google Tsguide > Google TypeScript Style Guide > Language features > Functions > Prefer function declarations for named functions

#### Prefer function declarations for named functions

Prefer function declarations over arrow functions or function expressions when defining named functions.

```
function foo() {
 return 42;
}
```
```
const foo = () => 42;
```
Arrow functions *may* be used, for example, when an explicit type annotation is
required.

```
interface SearchFunction {
 (source: string, subString: string): boolean;
}
const fooSearch: SearchFunction = (source, subString) => { ... };
```

